  "decision": {
    "bossTrimDB": -3,
    "reason": "The user reports a conspicuous Boss loudness increase. Existing full-file and loop integrated LUFS are already close, so repeating whole-file normalization would not address that feedback. Boss has a denser, less variable loudness profile (loop LRA 0.9 LU versus endless 2.4 LU); instantaneous transitions and perceived loudness are not guaranteed by integrated LUFS matching. Apply a deliberate, audible 3 dB playback balance correction to Boss only.",
    "qualification": "The measurements do not show a 3 dB full-track mismatch; the trim is a listening-feedback correction, not a claim that either original asset was normalized incorrectly. The first 10 seconds of Boss are already quieter on the integrated meter.",
    "runtimeRoute": "source -> static per-track trim -> normalized crossfade gain -> shared scene lowpass -> scene gain -> user BGM bus -> feedback duck -> master",
    "crossfadeSeconds": 0.65,
    "crossfadePolicy": "Keep normalized 0..1 equal-power automation separate from static trim, including rapid reversals; never normalize the static Boss correction away.",
    "loadingPolicy": "While Boss is pending, endless keeps its existing track/scene/bus gain. The trim exists before Boss source.start and affects only that source.",
    "scenePolicy": "Both endless and Boss play scenes remain gain 1 and cutoff 20000 Hz. Home/result attenuation, user BGM/SFX settings, mute and background controls are unchanged.",
    "lifecycle": "Retiring a faded-out Boss voice disconnects its source, static trim and crossfade gain; resident endless keeps its clock."
